# Responsive UI

Any UI change must work on **PC, laptop, tablet, and mobile**. Do not ship desktop-only layouts.

## Required checks

Before finishing UI work, verify (or adjust CSS for) roughly:

| Class | Width | Expectations |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Desktop | ?1280px | Sidebar, full content width, multi-column layouts |
| Laptop | 1024?1279px | Sidebar, fluid columns without overflow |
| Tablet | 640?1023px | Bottom navigation and More sheet; touch targets ?44px |
| Phone | ?639px | Single column, readable type, no page overflow |

Use the current 639px, 1023px and 1279px tiers in `journal.css` and `website/site.css`.
Also verify 360px phones, tablet landscape and 200% zoom. Update the stylesheet that
owns the component; avoid duplicating overrides across the legacy and journal layers.

## Patterns

```css
/* ❌ BAD — fixed width that breaks on phone */
.panel { width: 720px; }

/* ✅ GOOD — fluid + existing breakpoints */
.panel { width: 100%; max-width: 720px; }
@media (max-width: 639px) {
  .panel { padding: 12px; }
}
```

- Prefer fluid widths (`%`, `minmax(0, 1fr)`, `min-width: 0`) over fixed pixel shells.
- Stack grids/flex rows at tablet/mobile; don’t clip labels or force overflow.
- Modals, pickers, and toolbars must remain usable on small screens and touch (`hover: none`).
- When editing a component, update the matching `@media` rules in the owning stylesheet in the same change.
